From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joseph Telaak <joseph@telaak.dev>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 00:09:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] sf_smac: build against Linux 6.18 and cfg80211 7.2

The sf19a2890-6.9 branch was built against kernel 6.6. OpenWrt main
runs kernel 6.18 with the backports-7.2 wireless stack. Adapt the
driver to both:

cfg80211 (backports 7.2):
- add_key, get_key, del_key and set_default_mgmt_key take a
  wireless_dev; add, del, change, get and dump_station too.
  Internal callers pass dev->ieee80211_ptr.
- set_monitor_channel takes the net_device.
- set_wiphy_params, set_tx_power and get_tx_power take radio_idx;
  get_tx_power also takes link_id.
- remain_on_channel takes rx_addr.
- start_radar_detection and cfg80211_cac_event take link_id.
- cfg80211_rx_spurious_frame and cfg80211_rx_unexpected_4addr_frame
  take link_id; pass -1, as the driver does not do MLO.
- ieee80211_mgmt.u.action carries action_code next to category, no
  longer inside each sub-struct.
- ieee80211_amsdu_to_8023s takes mesh_control (the lite-memory path
  only).

Kernel 6.18:
- del_timer*() and from_timer() are gone; use timer_delete*() and
  timer_container_of().
- platform_driver.remove returns void.

While here, get_tx_power no longer reads a vif from an empty list when
it is called with no wdev.

Not compile-tested.

Signed-off-by: Joseph Telaak <joseph@telaak.dev>
